-- title:
--   Primes of Pl⊗ B as points of a chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbf Z/M)^\times$, and the hypothesis $hj$ that the Laurent series $jqModC$ over $\mathbf Q$ (namely $q^{-1}$ times the integral numerator series of $j$) lies in the $q$-expansion function field $qExpFunctionFieldC\ \mathbf Q\ \top$, the subfield of $\mathbf Q((q))$ generated by the integral form ratios at full level. Let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of the structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, which packages the proper flat integral normal model $X\ p\ (\Gamma_M M H)\ hj$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(R\ p)$ together with a curve model $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}$ over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ whose function field is identified with $xHFunctionFieldBar\ M\ H$ and an isomorphism $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{eeta}$ onto the base change of that model along $R\ p \to \overline{\mathbf Q}$. Let $Pl$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit in $Pl$, and let $\rho : R\ p \to Pl$ be a ring map compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ and realising the given $R\ p$-algebra structure on $Pl$. Let $B$ be an $R\ p$-subalgebra of $qExpFunctionFieldC\ \mathbf Q\ (\Gamma_M M H)$ and $\iota_B : \operatorname{Spec} B \to X\ p\ (\Gamma_M M H)\ hj$ an open immersion over $\operatorname{Spec}(R\ p)$, i.e. $\iota_B$ followed by $toBase$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R\ p \to B$. Assume the preimage under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{eeta}$ followed by the first pullback projection of the open image of $\iota_B$ is nonempty, and that each $b \in B$ is read on $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}$ as itself: the germ of the pullback of $b$ on that open, transported by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ into $xHFunctionFieldBar\ M\ H$, is the coefficientwise image $coeffEmb$ of the Laurent series of $b$. Finally let $\gamma : Pl \otimes_{R\,p} B \to xHFunctionFieldBar\ M\ H$ be a ring map with $\gamma(\alpha \otimes b)$ equal, as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, to $\alpha \cdot coeffEmb(b)$. The conclusion is threefold: $\gamma$ is injective; every $e \in xHFunctionFieldBar\ M\ H$ satisfies $e\,\gamma(s) = \gamma(a)$ for some $a, s$ with $s \ne 0$, so the function field is the field of fractions of the image of $\gamma$; and for every prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $Pl \otimes_{R\,p} B$ whose contraction along $\alpha \mapsto \alpha \otimes 1$ is $\bot$ and with $\mathfrak q \ne \bot$, there are a section $y$ of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbf Q}$ and a ring map $\chi : Pl \otimes_{R\,p} B \to \overline{\mathbf Q}$ such that $e$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\ y$ if and only if $e\,\gamma(s) = \gamma(a)$ for some $a$ and some $s \notin \mathfrak q$; $\chi$ restricted along $\alpha \mapsto \alpha \otimes 1$ is the inclusion $Pl \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbf Q}$; $\ker \chi = \mathfrak q$; and $y$ followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{eeta}$ and the first pullback projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\chi)$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}(b \mapsto 1 \otimes b)$ followed by $\iota_B$.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the scheme-theoretic and the valuation-theoretic descriptions of the geometric generic fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model along an affine $j$-chart: nonzero primes of $Pl \otimes_{R\,p} B$ lying over $(0) \subset Pl$ correspond to $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-points of the chart, the residue map being $\chi$, and the localisation at such a prime, read inside the function field through $\gamma$, is the valuation ring of the associated place. It feeds the statements about branch primes, crossing primes and reduction of sections at $p$ that use the chart to compare a place of the function field with a point of the model.
